index 78c0b92..7f3eb47 100644
--- a/docs/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/docs/DECISIONS.md
@@ -108,3 +108,4 @@ record for this repository; propose a change as a PR that adds a new entry
 | D-100 | 2026-10-27 | **The flare detector has its own page** (`web/flare_page.py`, `web/templates/web/product_detail_flare.html`), replacing the generic event page for `usach.flare.nrt`: current state (quiet / flare in progress / delayed / coming soon, from the latest event and the heartbeat), the 4 AIA channels as image or as the model's difference, the last 24 h of probability against GOES 0.1–0.8 nm flux, and the last 7 days of events with a GOES class taken from the stored X-ray peak in [start − 10 min, end + 10 min]. Everything is read from what the portal already stores, except the channel images: `productos/usach.flare.nrt/aia/<wave>.png` proxies Centella's `127.0.0.1` `/api/image/<wave>.png` (cached 60 s, 404 when the model is down; Centella stays unexposed, ARCHITECTURE §6). Charts are server-rendered SVG; the page reloads every 2 min with a meta refresh (no JS). | The mockup was approved; the generic page showed only the last event's issue time. | Nicolás / Claude |
 | D-101 | 2026-11-02 | **The flare page gets an "Explorar" companion** (`productos/usach.flare.nrt/explorar/`, `web/templates/web/product_detail_flare_explore.html`, `web/static/web/js/flare-explore.js`). It shows the same hero, 4 AIA channels (image / difference), Grad-CAM, and Centella-events vs GOES-flares tables, all driven by a time cursor over any period: a timeline in vendored ECharts with zoom, click to jump, playback and keyboard steps, and the instant kept in the URL hash. Its data come through whitelisted portal proxies to a Centella API (≥ 2.2): `explorar/datos/{range,series,events,flares}.json` (params `start`, `end`, `days` only), `explorar/datos/frame/<slot>.json`, `aia/<wave>.png?slot=` and `explorar/gradcam/<slot>.png`. A slot must match `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM[:SS]Z`. JSON is cached 30 s, slot images a day, and a source that is down gives 502/404. The source is `FLARE_ARCHIVE_URL` (`modules/flare/client.py`), which defaults to the live `FLARE_NRT_URL`; pointing it at a Centella API that serves a replayed period (e.g. a month on the processing server, through an SSH tunnel) makes the page an evaluation tool without touching the live page. The live page stays server-rendered with its meta refresh (D-100); the cursor-driven view needs JS, so it is a separate page linked from it. The disk marker now uses the synoptic field of view (1024 px × 2.4″) instead of an approximate 86 % disk. The producer repository is `HelioUSACH/flare-nrt` (maintainers' brief, 2026-10-28; supersedes the rename in D-099), with Centella as the model's name. | Owner asked to browse the month's replay in the page's design, frame by frame. | Nicolás / Claude |
 | D-102 | 2026-11-02 | **One flare page, with a time cursor** (supersedes D-101's separate page; `explorar/` now redirects to the page with `#fuente=archivo`). The first paint is still server-rendered from what the portal stores (D-100: state, latest images, 24 h SVG chart, recent events). `web/static/web/js/flare-page.js` then turns it into the time-cursor view. It follows "now" (polls every 60 s; the cursor stays on the newest frame until the reader moves it, and "Ahora" returns to it), goes back through any period, and switches source between the live service (`FLARE_NRT_URL`) and a replayed archive (`FLARE_ARCHIVE_URL`, offered only when it differs). Every proxy takes `fuente=vivo|archivo` and caches per source: `datos/{range,series,events,flares}.json`, `datos/frame/<slot>.json`, `aia/<wave>.png?slot=`, `gradcam/<slot>.png`. The GOES 0.1–0.8 nm flux comes from the portal's own `noaa.goes.xray` rows through `datos/xray.json` (window ≤ 14 days, ≤ ~2000 points), drawn on a log axis A–X as before. GOES flare bands come from Centella ≥ 2.2.1 `/api/flares`, which adds SWPC's 7-day list for recent days. Without JS the page keeps its 2-min reload (in `<noscript>`). | Owner asked for a single page: open on "now", go back in time, and browse the month's replay without a separate page. | Nicolás / Claude |
+| D-103 | 2026-11-04 | **Flare page redesign, from a reviewed mockup** (`product_detail_flare.html`, `flare-page.js`, the flare block of `base.css`; supersedes D-100/D-102's layout, not their data flow). Top: a dark `--space` band with the title "Flares solares", the source switch (En vivo / Archivo) and the cursor's time in large mono; in live it reads "Actualizado hace … · imagen de hace … min", in archive "Archivo de evaluación · first → last". The source/period form bar is gone. Hero, in three columns that stack on a phone: the state card, the 131 Å disk (131 Å / Diferencia / Grad-CAM) and the 4 channels in 2 × 2. The state card has one colour per Centella state (quiet / onset / active / decay from the series' `state`, plus "sin resultado" and, live only, "sin datos recientes"), a 4-step strip (Calma → Inicio → En curso → Decae), the probability with a last-hour sparkline, and three facts: AIA image, GOES class (the flare's, else the X-ray flux at that instant) and location. Location reads as Stonyhurst lat/lon plus arcsec (`flare_page.heliographic`, duplicated in JS: low-precision ephemeris for the solar radius and B0, ~1°; off-disk or on-limb regions keep arcsec only). The box on the disk carries a label ("M3.1 · N17 W29"). Timeline: two ECharts lanes sharing the time axis (probability with the 0.80 line; GOES on a log axis with M/X labels at their peaks), event bands across both, the cursor and its time; window 6 h / 24 h / 3 d / 7 d, plus "Todo" in archive. Archive also gets a strip of the whole period (max probability per bucket, alerts in red, the window framed; click moves the window). The transport sits under the chart (event jumps, ±1 image, play at 1×/2×/4×, position "imagen i de n", Ahora / Volver a en vivo). New: a summary of the *period* (last 24 h live, the whole archive up to 40 days otherwise): Centella events, M/X detected (and ≥ M2), max probability, false alarms, coverage, with Centella's validation rules (hit: an alert in [start − 10, end + 5] min; false alarm: no C-or-larger flare in [start − 10, end + 30] min). The two tables become one "Flares y alertas" list: each M/X flare with its alert (Detectada / No detectada) and each other alert (Alerta en flare C / Falsa alarma / En curso). Removed after review: subtitle, latency fact, captions under the disk and channels, channel descriptions (now a tooltip) and the "cómo leerlo" section. "flare" everywhere instead of "fulguración" on this page. No new endpoint: the period reuses `series`/`events`/`flares`, and windows inside the period are served from it. |
